# L §5.6 A stepped range: "a .. b step s of quantities, dates or durations (g in 0 PLN .. gross_cap step
# minor(PLN))"; L §5.18: "The least value that meets a condition ... is min(v for v in lo .. hi step u where c)
# over a stepped range".  With cap 10.00 PLN and target 3.01 PLN, the least g on the 0.01 PLN grid with
# g + g >= 3.01 PLN is 1.51 PLN (1.50 + 1.50 = 3.00 < 3.01).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

input cap: money PLN
input target: money PLN

def least: money PLN at reader
  rule base = min(g for g in 0 PLN .. cap step minor(PLN) where g + g >= target)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  cap = 10.00 PLN
  target = 3.01 PLN

ask q1: least law 2026-06-30
=== expect
q1: 1.51 PLN
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-01-01
